  "id": "COMPOUND:28103 - PROTEIN:5792",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that the compound [(2S,3R,4S,5S,6R)-6-[[(2R,3R,4R,5S,6R)-3,4-dihydroxy-6-(hydroxymethyl)-5-[(2S,3R,4R,5R,6S)-3,4,5-trihydroxy-6-methyloxan-2-yl]oxyoxan-2-yl]oxymethyl]-3,4,5-trihydroxyoxan-2-yl] (1R,3aS,5aS,5bR,7aR,8R,11aR,11bR,13aR,13bR)-8-(hydroxymethyl)-5a,5b,8,11a-tetramethyl-1-prop-1-en-2-yl-9-[(2R,3R,4S,5S,6R)-3,4,5-trihydroxy-6-(hydroxymethyl)oxan-2-yl]oxy-1,2,3,4,5,6,7,7a,9,10,11,11b,12,13,13a,13b-hexadecahydrocyclopenta[a]chrysene-3a-carboxylate) is a target of multiple compounds, including ent-Intermedeol, Polygalasaponin XXXIII, and [(1R,3R,4S,6S,8S,9R,10S,11S)-8-hydroxy-3,8-dimethyl-12-methylidene-9-(2-methylprop-2-enoyloxy)-7,13-dioxo-5,14-dioxatricyclo[9.3.0.04,6]tetradecan-10-yl] 2-methylprop-2-enoate. These compounds are all implicated in the regulation of RWLeu4, a target involved in cellular processes. The evidence suggests that the compound is a potential target for drugs that can modulate the activity of RWLeu4, possibly through interactions that involve hydroxymethyl groups, hydroxy groups, and oxan-2-yl moieties. The relationship between the compound and RWLeu4 is supported by multiple independent pathways, indicating a robust and well-documented interaction.",
